    "notes": "Corvus Store 5.0.1 rearranges the Store.\n\nThe Mods section is now Arcade. At the top a large banner shows the models' own artwork in turn, with the model's line and its button; below it you can show all models, only the ones you have installed, or only the ones with an update. Top Models lists every released model, numbered, in this order: Halia, OUKA, ASTRAEA, Cherry, Tsubomi, Noctua and Aureum. Noctua runs on Palworld servers, so the Store does not install it; its button opens its page on the website. It used to be listed as Coming soon, which was wrong: it has been out since 4 October. The retired Alpha follows underneath.\n\nThe new Work section holds Corvus Agent: its card to get, update or open it, and under it Corvus Studio (Dashboard, Activity, Settings) for the server it looks after. It takes the place of the Agents section, so there is still the same number of sections. Corvus Agent is no longer listed among the models; an update to it is offered on its card in Work.\n\nEverything else is 5.0.0.\n\nVerified: the unit tests pass (594, 474 and 149 in the three modules) with the compiler set to refuse any warning, including new tests that hold the order, keep Corvus Agent out of Arcade and check every language says Arcade and Work. The Store was drawn without a window in all 13 languages, and the new Arcade and Work screens were looked at in English, Japanese and Arabic (mirrored).\nNot verified, and worth saying: the banner's crossfade, hover and press have not been seen in a real window; nothing new was run on Windows; the words in the eleven languages other than English and Japanese were translated plainly and have not been read by a native speaker.",
